    "goal": "Size the binary .bed storage for a GWAS genotype dataset of 8232 samples and 9913735 variants, and report the per-chromosome file count and per-chromosome .bed size.",
    "rationale": "The binary PLINK .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant. Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome .bed size uses the same 2-bits rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (644433). The number of per-chromosome files corresponds to the number of chromosomes in a standard human reference build (25: 22 autosomes + X + Y + MT).",
